id: pm-sqvshj
title: "ADR: MCP 2026-07-28 is canonical and legacy interoperability is a bounded stateless adapter, not connection-local session state"
description: "Choose the protocol-version, transport, compatibility, and dependency strategy for replacing the 2025-06-18 initialize handshake without preserving forbidden session semantics."
type: Decision
status: open
priority: 1
tags[6]: adr,"area:mcp",compatibility,deprecation,protocol-versioning,stateless
created_at: "2026-08-25T05:07:23.485Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-25T05:07:23.485Z"
deadline: "2026-09-15T00:00:00.000Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "The accepted decision names canonical and supported legacy protocol versions plus a sunset policy; The decision resolves hand-rolled versus official-SDK usage while preserving the public pm SDK as the policy boundary; STDIO and Streamable HTTP negotiation, discovery, compatibility probes, and unsupported-version errors are specified; Every removed or deprecated feature has an explicit remove, adapt, or migrate disposition with security rationale; Rollout telemetry, negative controls, rollback, and released-artifact gates are defined before implementation starts"
goal: Interoperable current MCP without ambiguous dual semantics
objective: "Approve one explicit compatibility policy for 2026-07-28 core behavior, legacy clients, transports, extensions, and deprecations"
value: Implementation teams can migrate once against a stable architecture and test matrix
why_now: "Every downstream protocol child depends on whether initialize, ping, sessions, server-initiated requests, and legacy HTTP behavior remain adapters or are removed"
parent: pm-rs9vry
risk: critical
confidence: medium
