comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-25T05:07:23.485Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check evidence: searched all statuses for MCP protocol ADR 2026-07-28 stateless compatibility initialize removal and legacy adapters. pm-pif3 covers the old dependency-free implementation choice and pm-kl11 covers the old handshake test; neither decides the new revision."
body: "## Decision questions\n\n1. Canonical version and exact supported legacy versions.\n2. STDIO compatibility probe behavior when server/discover is unknown to an older client.\n3. Whether protocol support remains hand-rolled, adopts an official SDK, or isolates schema-derived wire contracts behind the public pm SDK.\n4. Streamable HTTP deployment and authorization scope.\n5. Removal or adapter policy for initialize, notifications/initialized, ping, logging/setLevel, roots changes, resource subscriptions, SSE resumability, and deprecated features.\n6. Capability and extension negotiation when a caller omits or conflicts with request metadata.\n7. Rollout, metrics, sunset criteria, and rollback without mutable history.\n\n## Preferred direction\n\nUse the official schema as the normative wire contract, keep transport-neutral semantics in the public pm SDK, make 2026-07-28 the default, and retain only explicitly tested compatibility adapters that do not recreate protocol-level sessions."
